<title>SWITZERLAND: Hungary settles farm subsidy dispute at WTO.</title>
<headline>Hungary settles farm subsidy dispute at WTO.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia, New Zealand, the United States and Argentina have settled their dispute with Hungary at the World Trade Organisation over Budapest's farm export subsidies, trade officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The complaint was the subject of a neutral panel set up by the global trade watchdog in February.</p>
<p>But trade officials said Australia told a meeting of the WTO's Dispute Settlement Body (DSB) on Wednesday that the complainants agreed to stop panel proceedings after Hungary agreed to seek a waiver on its agricultural restrictions.</p>
<p>The four had accused Hungary of breaching agricultural export subsidy curbs set during the Uruguay Round trade negotiations that ended in December 1993 under WTO's predecessor body, the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT).</p>
<p>--Geneva Newsroom 41-22-733 38 31</p>
